Files: src/save.c, src/restore.c, src/version.c, src/mdlib.c, src/files.c,
include/global.h, include/hack.h, util/sfctool.c

  o Only a seeded game's save file differs from NetHack 5.0's. It's marked
    by a feature bit of its own in the version info (SEEDED_GAME_BIT, set by
    store_version() for a seeded game's save file and checkpoint), and holds
    the seed data below at the start of its game state (savegamestate()).
    NetHack 5.0 doesn't know the bit, so it rejects such a file as a
    configuration it wasn't built with ("Configuration incompatibility"),
    whatever its VERSION_COMPATIBILITY; this fork lists the bit among the
    features it ignores when checking (md_ignored_features()), and
    uptodate() tells the restore whether the file has it (NHFILE's seeded
    field, which restgamestate() reads; check_version() changes nothing
    else). sfctool keeps the bit when it converts a file, and reads the
    seed data by it. An unseeded game's save file, and bones (seeded games
    make none), are the same as NetHack 5.0's, both ways.

  o The seed is saved with the game (gamestate-seed), with whether it was
    the server's hidden seed (gamestate-seedhidden). A restored game keeps
    its own seed, and stays hidden or not, whatever the option or sysconf
    says; a game started without a seed stays unseeded. If the option was
    ignored, the welcome message says so (for a hidden seed, whether the
    option happened to match it isn't let on). This stops a player restoring
    under a different seed to reroll unvisited levels, or restoring an
    unseeded game as a seeded one, and a hidden seed from being shown when
    its game is restored without SEED.

  o A saved seed is checked as the option's value is (B1), and must already
    be in canonical form; a save file whose seed isn't valid doesn't
    restore ("The saved game's seed isn't valid.").

  o A restore that fails at any stage leaves the game to start anew, from
    the seed sysconf and the options set (B3), not the one the failed
    restore read.

  o The game's seed generator version (gamestate-seedver) and every level's
    fingerprint (gamestate-levelhash) are saved too. A game's version is
    that of the build that started it, or the lowest of any build that has
    since restored it (nh_set_game_seedver()); that's the version shown and
    logged, and a restore by a build with another version gets a warning.

  o SEED_GEN_VERSION (currently 1) must be bumped whenever a change makes
    the same seed give a different dungeon.

  o Recovering a crashed game (recover_savefile(), when the player picks
    Recover) writes the save file's version info as the checkpoint has it,
    so a seeded game's checkpoint makes a seeded game's save file, whatever
    the options or sysconf say when it's recovered, and an unseeded one's
    an unseeded one's.


